{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "WPMS — Complaints",
    "description": "HTTP API for the Complaints module (`/v1/complaints`).\n\nImplemented operations:\n- **Create** — `POST /v1/complaints`\n- **Read (list)** — `GET /v1/complaints`\n- **Read (one)** — `GET /v1/complaints/:id`\n- **Update status** — `PATCH /v1/complaints/:id/status`\n\nStatus flow: `PENDING` → `UNDER_REVIEW` → `RESOLVED` (or `PENDING` → `RESOLVED`). `RESOLVED` is terminal.\n\nResponses are wrapped as `{ success, data, timestamp }`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000" },
    { "key": "complaintId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111" },
    { "key": "againstUserId", "value": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222" },
    { "key": "bookingId", "value": "33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Complaints",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Submit Complaint",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 or 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('success wrapper', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data).to.be.an('object');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.id).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.status).to.eql('PENDING');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (body && body.data && body.data.id) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('complaintId', body.data.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"userId\": \"{{userId}}\",\n  \"againstUserId\": \"{{againstUserId}}\",\n  \"bookingId\": \"{{bookingId}}\",\n  \"description\": \"Worker did not arrive at the scheduled time and was unreachable.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/complaints",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "complaints"]
            },
            "description": "Customer / Worker submits a complaint.\n\nRules:\n- `userId` ≠ `againstUserId`\n- `description` length 10–5000\n- Initial status: `PENDING`\n\nSaves `complaintId` from the response for later requests."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List Complaints",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('list payload shape', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.items).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.total).to.be.a('number');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/complaints?userId={{userId}}&againstUserId={{againstUserId}}&bookingId={{bookingId}}&status=PENDING&limit=20&offset=0",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "complaints"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "userId",
                  "value": "{{userId}}",
                  "description": "Filter by complainant UUID",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "againstUserId",
                  "value": "{{againstUserId}}",
                  "description": "Filter by accused user UUID",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "bookingId",
                  "value": "{{bookingId}}",
                  "description": "Filter by booking UUID",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "PENDING",
                  "description": "PENDING | UNDER_REVIEW | RESOLVED",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20",
                  "description": "1–100 (default 20)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "offset",
                  "value": "0",
                  "description": "≥ 0 (default 0)"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "List complaints with optional filters. Disable unused query params in Postman as needed.\n\nAdmin: omit filters or filter by status.\nCustomer/Worker: pass own `userId`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Complaint by ID",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('complaint returned', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('complaintId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/complaints/{{complaintId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "complaints", "{{complaintId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Get a single complaint by UUID. Run **Submit Complaint** first so `complaintId` is set."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Status — Under Review",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status is UNDER_REVIEW', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.status).to.eql('UNDER_REVIEW');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"UNDER_REVIEW\",\n  \"adminNote\": \"Assigned to support for investigation\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/complaints/{{complaintId}}/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "complaints", "{{complaintId}}", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Admin marks a `PENDING` complaint as `UNDER_REVIEW`.\n\nAllowed body `status`: `UNDER_REVIEW` | `RESOLVED`.\n`adminNote` optional (1–2000 chars)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Status — Resolved",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status is RESOLVED', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.status).to.eql('RESOLVED');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"RESOLVED\",\n  \"adminNote\": \"Refund issued and worker warned\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/complaints/{{complaintId}}/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "complaints", "{{complaintId}}", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Admin resolves a complaint (`PENDING` or `UNDER_REVIEW` → `RESOLVED`).\n\n`RESOLVED` is terminal — further status changes return 400."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Full complaint service surface as implemented in `ComplaintsController` / `ComplaintsService`.\n\nThere is no PUT full-update or DELETE endpoint — status changes are the only mutation after create."
    }
  ]
}
